window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-315e17f0f4b919c1"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"manage-chatgpt-space-pages-and-slides\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt-space\">管理 ChatGPT Space、页面和幻灯片</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p><span id=\"does-turning-off-library-file-sharing-remove-existing-access\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"how-should-we-handle-malicious-incoming-content\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"how-can-we-reduce-data-exfiltration-risk\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"is-enterprise-data-used-to-train-models\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-if-information-was-shared-unintentionally\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"what-is-chatgpt-space\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-space_1\">什么是 ChatGPT Space？</h2> <p>ChatGPT Space（以前称为 Library）汇集页面、幻灯片、上传的文件和共享内容，方便成员与智能体协作。团队可以起草文档、<a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=revise-the-content\">编辑页面</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">创建演示文稿</a>，或<a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a?anchor=start-with-a-bounded-request\">请 ChatGPT 修改内容</a>。</p> <p>产品使用说明请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">ChatGPT Space 指南</a>和<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">帮助中心关于 Library 文件的说明（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"enterprise-sharing-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">企业共享控制</h2> <p>使用<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-and-edu-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">共享 Library 文件和文件夹（需联网）</a>，在<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">工作区和角色层级</a>管理共享。关闭共享功能会阻止新建共享和更改权限，但不会撤销已有共享访问权限。用户仍可创建和查看私人内容。</p> <p>仅有 Admin 角色并不代表拥有<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001067-data-access-for-your-managed-chatgpt-account\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">敏感合规数据访问权限（需联网）</a>。如需通过受支持的端点<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">导出或删除符合条件的已保存 Library 文件（需联网）</a>，必须具备 <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=get-started\">Compliance API 权限</a>。</p> <p><span id=\"what-if-a-file-will-not-save-or-upload\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"help-users-create-and-share-pages\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">帮助用户创建和共享页面</h2> <p>用户可以<a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=draft-your-first-page\">创建页面</a>，并<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=share-a-page-or-space\">与人员或可用的工作区团队共享</a>，同时选择查看或编辑权限。</p> <p>共享页面不会公开私人聊天或已保存的记忆。添加到页面上的私人详细信息会对协作者可见。</p> <p>上传内容会遵循页面权限。链接到页面的源文件保留各自的权限。复制或概述到页面中的内容则会对页面协作者可见。</p> <p><a id=\"help-users-create-and-share-slides\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">帮助用户创建和共享幻灯片</h2> <p>ChatGPT Slides 允许成员在 Space 中与 ChatGPT 和队友一起创建、编辑演示文稿。Slides 使用与 Space 和页面相同的访问设置。工作区共享说明请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001544-chatgpt-space-sharing-data-and-controls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Space 共享、数据与控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>成员可以授予他人查看或编辑幻灯片的权限。拥有编辑权限的成员可共同修改同一份幻灯片，并在共享评论中讨论更改。有关权限和反馈，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=collaborate-on-slides\">协作编辑幻灯片</a>。</p> <p>如果 Windows 桌面应用创建的是 PowerPoint 文件，而不是协作演示文稿，请引导成员切换到云端模式或在 ChatGPT 网页版中操作。完整流程请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">创建并完善幻灯片</a>；平台要求请参阅帮助中心的 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001605\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中创建和协作编辑幻灯片（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"plugins-and-connected-accounts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">插件与已连接账户</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=overview\">插件</a>可以提供应用、技能或两者兼有。安装插件本身并不会授权其应用访问数据。</p> <p>请设置<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-2-manage-capabilities\">应用可用性、角色访问权限和允许执行的操作</a>。应用能够访问哪些内容取决于已连接账户的权限；<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">审批设置（需联网）</a>则决定 ChatGPT 何时会在执行操作前征求确认。</p> <p><a id=\"governance-and-data-protection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">治理与数据保护</h2> <p>OpenAI 默认不会使用 ChatGPT Enterprise 数据训练模型。已保存的 Library 文件遵循工作区的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8983778-chat-and-file-retention-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">保留策略（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>请限制共享和应用操作，并在支持的情况下要求对重要操作进行审批。<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/mcp.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">只读查询</a>仍可能向外部服务披露数据。页面、文件和工具结果可能包含<a href=\"https://openai.com/safety/prompt-injections/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">提示注入（需联网）</a>，试图误导 ChatGPT 或诱导其泄露信息。安全措施可以降低风险，但无法完全消除风险。</p> <p><a id=\"faq\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">常见问题</h2> <p><a id=\"space\"></a> <strong>共享项目能否使用个人 Space 文件？</strong></p> <p>共享项目时，个人 Space 文件会从项目来源中移除，但原始文件不会被删除。直接上传到项目的文件仍可供项目成员使用。另请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10169521-projects-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的项目（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><strong>删除内容后会发生什么？</strong></p> <p>删除页面或 Space 后，该内容及其嵌套页面会移至“废纸篓”。单独保存在 Space 中的文件不会因为聊天或项目被删除而一并消失。关于已保存文件的删除方式，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">管理 Library 文件（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"-1\"></a> <strong>成员离开工作区后会发生什么？</strong></p> <p><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266418-data-retention-when-a-member-is-removed-from-a-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">移除成员（需联网）</a>后，其工作区访问权限会立即撤销；保留的 Enterprise 聊天和文件仍遵循工作区保留策略。<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">断开应用连接（需联网）</a>会停止该连接今后的访问，但不会自动删除已保存的内容。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"manage-chatgpt-space-pages-and-slides\">Manage ChatGPT Space, pages, and slides</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p><span id=\"does-turning-off-library-file-sharing-remove-existing-access\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"how-should-we-handle-malicious-incoming-content\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"how-can-we-reduce-data-exfiltration-risk\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"is-enterprise-data-used-to-train-models\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"what-if-information-was-shared-unintentionally\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"what-is-chatgpt-space\">What is ChatGPT Space?</h2> <p>ChatGPT Space (formerly Library) brings together pages, slide decks, uploaded files, and shared content so people and agents can collaborate. Teams can draft documents, <a href=\"#/article/a-c7393fbab700d02d?anchor=revise-the-content\">edit pages</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">create presentations</a>, or <a href=\"#/article/a-2d083870d670ea3a?anchor=start-with-a-bounded-request\">ask ChatGPT for revisions</a>.</p> <p>For product guidance, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-9eaf251f273c9bc9\">ChatGPT Space guide</a> and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Help Center guidance on Library files (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"enterprise-sharing-controls\">Enterprise sharing controls</h2> <p>Use <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10128477-chatgpt-enterprise-and-edu-release-notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Share Library files and folders (online)</a> to manage sharing at the <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=set-the-workspace-default-then-create-targeted-custom-roles\">workspace and role level</a>. Disabling sharing blocks new shares and permission changes, but existing shared access remains. Users can still create and view private content.</p> <p>An Admin role alone does not grant <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001067-data-access-for-your-managed-chatgpt-account\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sensitive compliance access (online)</a>. <a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0?anchor=get-started\">Compliance API permissions</a> are required to <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">export or delete eligible saved Library files (online)</a> through supported endpoints.</p> <p><span id=\"what-if-a-file-will-not-save-or-upload\"></span></p> <h2 id=\"help-users-create-and-share-pages\">Help users create and share pages</h2> <p>Users can <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=draft-your-first-page\">create a page</a> and <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=share-a-page-or-space\">share it with people or available workspace teams</a>, choosing view or edit access.</p> <p>Sharing a page keeps private chats and saved memory private. Private details added to the page are visible to its collaborators.</p> <p>Uploads follow the page’s permissions. Linked source files retain their own permissions. Content copied or summarized onto a page is visible to its collaborators.</p> <h2 id=\"help-users-create-and-share-slides\">Help users create and share slides</h2> <p>ChatGPT Slides lets members create and edit presentations in Space with ChatGPT and their teammates. Slides uses the same access setting as Space and pages. For workspace sharing guidance, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001544-chatgpt-space-sharing-data-and-controls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Space sharing, data, and controls (online)</a>.</p> <p>Members can share a deck with view or edit access. People with edit access can revise the same deck together and discuss changes in shared comments. See <a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=collaborate-on-slides\">Collaborate on slides</a> for permissions and feedback.</p> <p>If the Windows desktop app creates a PowerPoint file instead of a collaborative deck, direct the member to cloud mode or ChatGPT on the web. For the full workflow, see <a href=\"#/article/a-71293722d815f9b8?anchor=create-and-refine-slides\">Create and refine slides</a>. For platform requirements, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001605\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and collaborating on slides in ChatGPT (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <h2 id=\"plugins-and-connected-accounts\">Plugins and connected accounts</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=overview\">Plugins</a> can provide apps, skills, or both. Installing a plugin does not authorize its apps.</p> <p>Set <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-2-manage-capabilities\">app availability, role access, and allowed actions</a>. The connected account’s permissions determine what it can access; <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001495-managing-app-permissions-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">approval settings (online)</a> determine when ChatGPT asks before an action.</p> <h2 id=\"governance-and-data-protection\">Governance and data protection</h2> <p>OpenAI does not train on ChatGPT Enterprise data by default. Saved Library files follow the workspace’s <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8983778-chat-and-file-retention-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">retention policy (online)</a>.</p> <p>Limit sharing and app actions, and require approval for consequential actions where supported. <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/mcp.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Read-only queries</a> can still disclose data to external services. Pages, files, and tool results may contain <a href=\"https://openai.com/safety/prompt-injections/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">prompt injections (online)</a> that redirect ChatGPT or disclose information. Safeguards reduce, but do not eliminate, this risk.</p> <h2 id=\"faq\">FAQ</h2> <p><a id=\"can-a-shared-project-use-personal-space-files\"></a> <strong>Can a shared project use personal Space files?</strong></p> <p>Sharing a project removes personal Space files from its sources without deleting the originals. Files uploaded directly to the project remain available to members. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/10169521-projects-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Projects in ChatGPT (online)</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-when-content-is-deleted\"></a> <strong>What happens when content is deleted?</strong></p> <p>Deleting a page or Space moves it and its nested pages to Trash. Files saved separately in Space remain when a chat or project is deleted. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001052-using-library-to-manage-files-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Library file management (online)</a> for saved-file deletion details.</p> <p><a id=\"what-happens-when-someone-leaves-the-workspace\"></a> <strong>What happens when someone leaves the workspace?</strong></p> <p><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8266418-data-retention-when-a-member-is-removed-from-a-workspace\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Removing a member (online)</a> immediately revokes workspace access; retained Enterprise chats and files follow workspace retention policy. <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Disconnecting an app (online)</a> stops future access through that connection but does not automatically delete saved content.</p>"};
